[17:11:24] I've redrawn the beetle as a Solo48 model and `validate_icon()` passes with no warnings. Most metric issues are fixed. When I ran the pipeline's metrics script on the redraw, it still reported two: 7 strokes instead of 6, and a head/shell contact it misreads as a clearance error.

**Drawing:** a side-view beetle on the suggested `HRECT_M` keyshape. The coiled shell is a single spiral that also forms the outline of the body: a large arc over the top, a lower arm under the body, then a small inner curl. I based this on how Lucide's snail builds its spiral from half-circle arcs, but spaced the turns 9 apart instead of letting them touch. The round head touches the shell at the front (as in the generated image), two antennae fan out from one point on the head, and there are three legs.

**Dropped from the image:**
- **Fourth leg:** four legs with the required 8 units between them don't fit under the shell, so I drew three, which is also what a real side view shows.
- **Knees:** a leg on the far right can't bend outward without leaving the keyshape box, so all legs are straight.

**Metric issues:**

| Issue | Result |
|---|---|
| Front leg 4.1 from the head | Fixed: now 8.6 |
| Antennae crowding each other and the shell (3 pairs) | Fixed: they share one root and spread 63°, so the tips are 8+ apart and 8+ from the shell |
| Paired legs 4–5 apart | Fixed: three legs, 8+ apart |
| Spiral fused into the shell wall at 13.8°, and 4 spiral clearances | Fixed: the spiral and shell are now one continuous line, so no separate spiral meets the wall |
| Holes 5.6 and 4.56 wide (need 6) | Fixed: the head's inner hole measures 5.88 and the script now passes it; the shell interior opens into the spiral, so it no longer forms a closed hole |
| Antenna 0.38 short of the head | Fixed: they now start exactly on the head |
| Keyshape only 96% wide | Fixed: the drawing touches all four sides of the box exactly |
| Trace stroke thinner than 4 (info) | Drawn at stroke 4, with all gaps sized for it |
| **9 strokes, budget 6** | **Only reduced to 7.** Merging the antennae into one V-shaped stroke gives 6, but then the script no longer sees the antennae touching the head and reports a false clearance error. |
| **Head/shell reported 0 apart** | **Not fixable.** The head is meant to touch the shell; the contact is declared as a connection and the validator accepts it. The script only recognises contact at the ends of lines, and here the head meets the middle of the shell's line, so it counts as an error. |

**Visual check:** I looked at it at 48 px on light and dark backgrounds. The spiral and antennae read clearly. Two weaker points: the head is small, and the rear leg carries straight on from the end of the shell's line, so at 48 px it can look like a snail-like creature more than a beetle. The generated image is ambiguous in the same way.

As you asked, the module isn't registered under `icon_set/model/icons`, `published/` is untouched, and I didn't run the build, tests or gallery.

Files are in `new-pipeline-test/output_png/20260928-1657-beetle-in-coiled-shell/`:
- `beetle_in_coiled_shell_redraw.py`
- `beetle-in-coiled-shell_redraw.svg`
- `beetle-in-coiled-shell_redraw.png`
- `beetle-in-coiled-shell_redraw-48.png`

